From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:29:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] docked-manager: The OSK stays on when docked

Plinius: the desktop over VNC adds a second screen and a pointer, so
Phosh docks. Docking turned org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications
screen-keyboard-enabled off, and the phone had no OSK any more, not even
for a PIN prompt on its own panel, until the desktop ended.

The docked mode leaves that setting alone now. phoc keeps the OSK on the
built-in panel and only unfolds it for fields shown there, so the
desktop's windows are still typed into with the PC's keyboard.
---
 src/docked-manager.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/docked-manager.c b/src/docked-manager.c
index 35d97dfc..da649a1f 100644
--- a/src/docked-manager.c
+++ b/src/docked-manager.c
@@ -304,7 +304,9 @@ phosh_docked_manager_set_enabled (PhoshDockedManager *self, gboolean enable)
   /* we could bind one boolean property via g_settings_bind but that would spread
    * mode setup over several places */
   g_settings_set_boolean (self->phoc_settings, PHOC_KEY_MAXIMIZE, !enable);
-  g_settings_set_boolean (self->a11y_settings, A11Y_KEY_OSK, !enable);
+  /* Plinius: the OSK stays on when docked. The second screen is the desktop over VNC, the phone
+   * keeps its own panel and needs the OSK there (PIN prompts, apps on the phone); phoc only
+   * unfolds it for fields on the built-in panel and keeps it there */
   if (self->gtk_settings)
     g_settings_set_boolean (self->gtk_settings, GTK_KEY_IS_PHONE, !enable);
   if (self->gtk4_settings)
